    "signature": "One const pointer to a packed image; unsigned 16/32/64-bit offset result. No frontend inline assembly.",
    "effects": "One instruction owns image read, selector checks, hidden segment installation and descriptor accessed-bit writes. Exact volatile image read and separate unknown volatile descriptor read/write MMOs; implicit segment definitions, scheduling boundaries, unchanged arithmetic flags.",
    "mode_guards": "LDS/LES require 32-bit code; 64-bit results require long mode; code16 refused. NeverC does not advertise LDS/LES C builtins and diagnoses their IR on its x64 backend.",
    "neverd": "Strict and permissive far-pointer lifting remain refused. Coupled offset/selector/hidden state and original-instruction continuation are still missing.",
    "caller": "Maintain compiler ABI segment invariants. No automatic TLS restoration or stack switching. Original addressing/segment/default-stack provenance and LSS successor adjacency are not represented."
